## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Reading Director's recut from `VID-animatic` v03 content/shot_list** — failed because: STALE artifact. shot_list said sequential sh01-26; content markdown said a DIFFERENT reorder; NEITHER matched his UI. Real source of truth = `episode.metadata.excluded_shot_ids`. Lesson: the online editor's exclusions/order persist to episode.metadata, not the animatic asset.
- **`/api/media/<music>.mp3` fetch** — failed because: returns HTTP 307 redirect (86-byte stub), not the file. Used old `VID-final_cut` mp4's baked audio instead (reliable).
- **node writing to git-bash path `/c/Users/...`** — failed because: Windows node read it as `C:\c\Users\...`. Fix: pass Windows path with forward slashes `C:/Users/...`.
- **`videos.list` on old short `8afgQAWP9ac`** — returns 0 items (Director deleted it). Fine.
- **First avatar SendUserFile / video preview (41MB)** — failed because: exceeded 30MB SendUserFile limit. Fix: re-encode preview at CRF 31 veryfast → 12.5MB.
- **ffmpeg preview at `-preset medium`** — timed out at 2min. Fix: `-preset veryfast`.

